WEBVTT

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.930
Why am I doing this again?

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.270
This is backbreaking...

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.750
Sure looks like they're enjoying themselves.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.280
Haku, let's have this done by lunch, okay?

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.450
Yeah, can do.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.790
Excuse me, coming through.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.350
What's that about?

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.810
Hard at work, I see.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:06.980
Why, you...

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.920
This wasn't the deal.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.670
What do you mean?

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.920
Wasn't this supposed to be a secret mission?

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.930
I want you two to protect the capital and its people in my place.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.220
What?

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.680
You must have a very high opinion of us.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.310
I'd like to think I'm a good judge of character.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.740
What are you talking about?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.300
Protect the capital?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.690
What exactly does that involve?

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.700
I'll give you the details when the time is right.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.450
You will be getting your 
hands dirty, perhaps even...

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.830
You may be forced to disavow us.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.960
"You will die, and no one will come for your corpse."

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.460
That's what a secret mission as 
General of the Right entails, correct?

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.220
You'll be paid, of course.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.330
This is enough to get you started.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.900
Uh, money's not the issue...

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.100
Okay, sure.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.220
Wait, Kuon!

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.160
Let's do it, Haku!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.230
It sounds fun.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.480
Fun?

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:04.140
I thought you'd just want us to quietly get rid of evil merchants and corrupt bureaucrats.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.990
Nasty problems like that are few and far between.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.320
But it happens sometimes, huh?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.240
Don't sweat the details!

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.750
Stop hitting me.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.000
Come join me, Nekone!

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.750
Okay, Big Sister!

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.250
Looks like Nekone's taken a liking to the young miss.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.710
{And all the obnoxious traits are rubbing off onto her.}{orig: And it's made her even more obnoxious.}{Here Haku is saying that there's another loud person around him now, telling him what to do}And now I've got two bossy girls to deal with.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.760
Shouldn't you take her home?

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.100
It's easier to wise her up when she's here.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.880
That's pretty harsh for a big brother.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.120
"Spare the rod, spoil the child," and all that.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.770
You should hang around a bit longer, too. Okay?

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.030
Fine.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.530
The jobs we have now are...

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.850
Manning a merchant's stall 
and carrying cargo, right?

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.280
And also repairing a roof.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:54.040
These feel more like odd jobs than secret missions.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.790
Either way, a steady stream of work is never a bad thing.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.450
Well maybe, but...

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.720
We got that money from Ukon, right?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.500
With a sum that big, surely we can live easy for a while, right?{orig: If we've got all that, we don't have to work so hard, do we?}

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.040
It's all gone.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:13.480
What!?

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.170
I established this place as 
our base of operations.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.710
That's where all the money went.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.490
Not even a bit left?

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.470
Nope.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.590
You could've gotten a cheaper inn!

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.090
My big sister's decision{-making} was sound.{maybe just decision}

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.260
At an inn like Hakuroukaku,

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:37.710
there's no risk of the guests' secrets getting out.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.710
It's well-guarded in case of emergencies,

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:45.710
and the owner supposedly wields a great deal of influence around these parts.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.470
It's the perfect place to establish
a secret base of operations.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.470
Don't doubt this big sister of mine!

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.970
Oh, you're making me blush!{Oh, stop it, you! << IS THIS TOO MEME}

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:55.970
Yeah, I'm <i>sure</i> that's the reason why.{orig: Those all sound like good reasons, but...}{QQ: I'm gonna add some strong sarcasm here. don't like it? TOO BAD}

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.480
It <i>definitely</i> wasn't for the bath, or anything.{orig: You guys are just here for the baths, right?}

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.090
Let's have a meeting about our next job.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:01.940
Yes, let's.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.440
Honestly, you two...

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.440
And these are for you, Haku.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.960
It's time for you to learn how to read and write.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.210
Why?

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.230
What did I do to deserve this?{orig: Why do I have to keep living like this?}

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.830
Haku,

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.970
how's it going?

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.600
You've gotten through so much already!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.970
At this rate, there'll be nothing left to teach you.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:52.650
Is it just me, or are the piles getting taller every day?

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.790
How did it come to this?

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.720
How are you doing, Haku-san?

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.120
That's pretty good.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.120
<i>It's all correct.</i>

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.880
<i>I'm starting to understand what my brother saw in him.{lit. "So big brother also saw this in him". I think it's fine as it is right now, but I felt like CR's original was slightly off so}{It's fine :) }</i>

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:08.390
What's wrong?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.970
Oh, nothing.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:12.880
I'll go get some more advanced material.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.950
Don't give me more work to do!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.780
All right! I've done enough for today.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.140
I've worked hard.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.970
This is a good place to stop—

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.090
Haku-sama.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.910
I've brought you some tea.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.310
Oh, thanks.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.670
Don't push yourself too hard, okay?

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:45.400
You're right.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.420
I should take a break...

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.680
I guess I'll keep at it a bit longer.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.460
You're such a hard worker, Haku-sama.

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:06.690
Good work today.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.690
You actually managed to finish all of it?

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:11.930
Yeah...

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.840
So, about tomorrow's schedule...

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.160
Now look here, Kuon!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.860
{A guy can die if he works too much!}{WZ1:}A guy could die from being overworked!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.860
I was thinking you could have a day off.{QQ: this isn't a "kana" thing SO DON'T BUG ME ABOUT IT}

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.510
If he doesn't rest every now and then...

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:22.950
A day off ?

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:23.660
Yup.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.960
You've earned it.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.510
Kuon...

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.710
And here.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.550
Go relax and have fun tomorrow.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.720
O-Okay...

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.720
The amount's nothing to cry over, really...

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.220
So this is what they call 
"the fruits of one's labor"?{So this is the joy that labor brings, huh?}

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.480
There you are, young miss.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.950
Ukon!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.110
What is it?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.790
Free at the moment?

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.870
It's urgent.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.290
Here you go!

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.010
Food bought with money I worked hard to earn myself, huh?

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.960
That just makes it even more enticing!

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.390
All right, I'm gonna eat this with all the gratitude in my heart...

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:30.770
No, wait... Three-second rule...

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.570
Sorry.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.780
I was in a bit of a rush, y'see.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.030
You there!

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:38.530
Out of the way!

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:39.660
Watch out!

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.420
Halt, or the next arrow shall find your heart.{orig: Stop there, or the next one won't miss.}

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.930
Hand over the girl.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.930
Can you not hear me?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.000
I'm gonna live with him now!

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.820
I've lost the will to live...

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:14.990
You will not.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.070
Let us return home.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.700
I don't wanna go back.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.200
Is there no way to turn it back?

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.950
I'd rather die than go back!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.200
Why even live...

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:32.460
This is my duty.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:33.560
Oh, my.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.610
You're being aimed at, mister.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.380
Huh? What?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.630
Mister, you'd better run if you don't wanna get hit.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:47.060
Rurutie, you stay here.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:51.060
I need you to tell Haku about the mission when he gets back.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.810
I will. Please take care.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.570
Big Sister, I'll accompany you.

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:57.820
All right.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.570
A search this urgent {looks to be}must be a pretty serious matter.{looks to be is too wordy for a quick line like this, gomen qqwerty}

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.940
Woohoo!

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.580
We got away all clean-like.{QQ: going for da authentic hillbilly without shit like "Ah" instead of "I" and overusing apostrophes cos that looks like shit}{orig: Looks like we got away.}

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.220
Sorry you got tangled up in this here mess.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:24.340
Hey!

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.440
No need to be shy.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.350
Your handsome little face's a tad ruined...

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.270
Mister.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:32.300
What?

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:35.100
Well, from the <i>back</i> you looked pretty fine.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.110
That's a pretty mean thing to say...

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.370
Why was that man chasing you?

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:48.370
No lass likes a man too nosy for his own good.{orig: Girls don't like guys who ask questions.}

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.250
Really now?

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:49.870
Bye.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.120
I was just messin' around!

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.730
Don't try to change the subject.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.630
Are you a runaway?

00:11:56.630 --> 00:12:00.510
I just decided to secretly live all independent-like!

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.190
That's called being a runaway!

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:04.880
I just wanted a brief spell of freedom!

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.320
Then that guy back there...

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.520
He was sent by my dad to bring little ol' me back.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.520
Maybe you should just go home, then?

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.480
But y'see...

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:19.270
There's something I gotta do.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.530
Which is?

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.280
Y'see, {I've...}

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:28.030
I've come to fall in love!{I've come to fuck dudes and chew bubblegum, and I'm all outta bubblegum.}

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.040
Huh?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.340
I'm right here in the mighty capital,

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:37.610
so I wanna find a passionate love to set my heart ablaze!{orig: Since I'm actually here in the capital, 
I want to find a love so hot it burns me!}

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.670
{Correction: I will find love!}{Wouldn't mind the colon with a good pause,  but there isn't one so this needs reworded.}Or rather, I <i>will</i> find love!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.670
Life's fleetin', so fall in love, young maidens!

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.180
I see. Good luck with that.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.130
Don't be all grumpy like that!

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.300
Come look for love with me!

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:53.930
Let me go!

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:57.760
Won't you show this poor ol' lass around, mister?

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.440
Pretty please?

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.870
Do it, and I'll go home without a word.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.950
Just for today, got it?

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:17.280
"Top Hundred Best Spots for Couples in the Capital"...

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:18.960
This here book says

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.420
if two lovers write their names down on a piece of paper and tie it on this bridge,

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.710
their love will be fulfilled.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.160
What's your name, mister?

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.220
Haku.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:30.590
Haku?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.220
Sure is a pretty name.

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.760
Is it?

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:39.140
I'll just tie it to this here bridge...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.480
That was close.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:44.890
Here.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:49.500
What's wrong?

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:50.970
Nothin'!

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:58.300
Lovers who eat this candy together 
will live happily ever after!

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.000
Two, if you please, mister.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.920
Here you go.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.670
It's a gigiri?

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.170
Perfect for someone here with a girl.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.930
What happened to lovers living happily ever after?

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:16.650
Link our arms like so, and then we both...

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.120
Wh-Why do I hafta eat it with you?

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.820
It was your idea.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:34.240
If you touch this door together 
and swear your eternal love...

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.080
C'mon, you're blocking the road.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.660
It's okay now.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:44.410
What's wrong?

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:48.840
{My kokoro is mada junbi.}{Just gimme a moment.}{orig: Give me a second.}{mada kokoro no junbi ga}Wait... a moment...

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.750
You're a real good sport, mister.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.630
No way I can leave a girl who wants to fall in love by herself, right?

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:08.860
I'd feel pretty guilty if you got tricked by some weirdo.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.150
I reckon I've a good eye for honest men.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:14.620
You're a good person, after all.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.840
Sheesh...

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.870
So, are we done?

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.870
Indulge me a little while longer, okay?

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:24.880
There's still more?

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.380
Just a teensy while, please?

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.620
Just a little.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.790
Thanks.

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:42.500
From the side, you look kinda cool, I guess.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.640
Shut up.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.400
Find anything?

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:50.790
Yes, there was someone who saw her.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.400
They said she was with a suspicious person.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.910
We'd best hurry.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.580
This guy cleaned out my drainage ditch a while ago.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.560
He was a huge help.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.180
He fixed my roof, too.

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:07.770
Now even when the rainy 
season{long rains} arrives, I'll be fine.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:10.920
I don't know who he was, 
but he was a big help!

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:15.100
Are they talking about the Righteous Man?

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.360
The Righteous Man?

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.550
Yep.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.140
He hears the people's voices, no matter how small,

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:25.460
and helps them as if he were sent by the mighty Emperor himself.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.060
They say he's a top-secret agent of the Emperor,

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:30.690
or maybe even the royal general's personal attendant.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.980
Is he famous?

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.290
Famous enough that there's rumors about him, y'know?

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:36.450
I see.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:39.280
I'm sure he's a fine-looking gentleman!

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.040
I'd love to make his acquaintance!

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:44.080
Hey!

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.460
What was that for?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.970
You reveal yourself at last.{I've finally found you.}

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.420
You're...

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.910
You're quite the persistent one, aren't you?

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:03.840
<i>You</i> will stay where you are, sir.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.480
Will you come with me?

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.480
Guess it's time to throw in the towel.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:10.830
Wait.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.980
Hey, you recognize this guy?

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:16.490
Can't really say, what with his face all covered like that.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.490
So he's got a reason to hide his face, huh?

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.000
Did he really come to take you back?

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.210
Huh?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.000
Wh-What nonsense is this?

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:33.640
We can't trust a guy who won't even show his face!

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.970
Think about it!

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:36.760
Hey, hey! Who are you?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.490
I'm, uh... My brother...

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:45.270
I mean, I am under the strict orders of someone to bring her back!

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:48.000
He just said "brother," didn't he?

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.320
He sure did.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:50.770
I did not!

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.960
You said you wanted to bring her back,

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.460
but you're actually going to ransom her, aren't you?

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.030
Are you a kidnapper?

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:58.530
I am not!

00:17:58.530 --> 00:17:59.910
Haku!

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:01.070
Hey.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.410
What are you doing here?

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:05.100
Oh, uh...

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.920
I'm a little busy, actually.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.670
Well, well, mister.

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.560
What's that look supposed to mean?

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:16.170
Got ourselves a missus, do we?

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.180
Huh?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.930
No?

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.630
Nope.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.680
Our relationship's not like that.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:28.000
Aw, that's no fun.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.690
Here I was, hoping to get myself some advice.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.690
Advice on what?

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.310
What else?

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:39.450
If you're lovers, you must be doing <i>all kinds</i> of raunchy things with one another!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.670
Not even close.{lol I just read WZ1's qc and he had the italics move too, so yeah}

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:43.450
"<i>All kinds</i> of raunchy things"?

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.360
How sweet!

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:50.030
Um... Are you guys done?

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:52.470
Big Sister, you've found her?

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.960
Nekone-san?

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.340
I don't know anyone suspicious like you.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:01.090
It's me, Kiuru!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.850
Oh, you two know each other?

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:14.110
So you're saying Oshutoru 
asked you to find Atui, too?

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:18.980
My brother told me to keep my 
intentions secret from the public.{Secret from general public}

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.110
That's why I...

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:24.410
Did you not realize a mask would
just make you stand out more?

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:28.620
You're right, Nekone-san.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.400
This is a lot of trouble over one runaway girl.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.520
I can understand why.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:39.240
I thought she was the daughter of some merchant, but she's not.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.130
She's probably...

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:47.140
She is Atui-sama, daughter of 
Soyankekuru-sama, the Ouro of Shahhoro.{what the fuck is an Ouro}{well rip}

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:48.640
It's a pleasure.

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:51.390
You're a princess. Don't run away from home.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.420
Love was waiting for me!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:59.040
But I'll go back to the palace.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.150
I can't keep being a bother to you all.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.590
Oh, and mister?

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.410
What is it?

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:11.180
Thanks for today!

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.000
Heard you were the star player today.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.670
Oh, lay off.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:27.680
So I heard about this 
"Righteous Man" in town today.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:33.500
He hears the voices of the people, 
no matter how small,

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:36.440
and takes on trivial work the royal general can't.{lit. "something royal generals can't do". He's saying that royal general is too important to go around helping people for things so small}

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.190
Why are you doing this?

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:42.070
To see the people through good and bad.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:44.700
That's what I want.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.890
I see.

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:04.090
Just until I find another job with good pay, okay?

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:05.430
Right.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:20.290
My brother... No, Oshutoru-sama told me to help you.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:21.470
I am Kiuru.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:23.760
Everyone! Nekone-san!

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.490
I look forward to working with you all.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:26.840
Sure.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.090
Yeah.

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.540
Nice to meet you too.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:32.800
I look forward to working with you...

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.250
As formal as always.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.560
I look forward to working with you all.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.250
What's this about?

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.860
Hey, cool-looking mister!

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:46.040
What are you doing here?

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:48.400
I'm moving in, so I thought I'd say my hellos.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.540
You're moving in?

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:51.470
My room's right next to yours.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.010
N-Next to mine?

00:21:56.090 --> 00:21:57.270
Seriously...

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:00.020
I'll be seeing you 'round!
